## 6. Cache-Warming Process

After connecting to the newly started LDAP container, perform the LDAP cache-warming procedure

The cache-warming commands are maintained on the [LDAP - Data migration and cutover from legacy environment to MP confluence page](https://dsdmoj.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/NH/pages/4589715816/LDAP+-+Data+migration+and+cutover+from+legacy+environment+to+MP#4.-Queries-to-run-to-warm-up-LDAP-server-and-preload-cache-entries)

They are also listed below for your reference:

```
# query to get all user entries into cache
# needs root password — this is passed from the environment using `-w` flag
# alternatively, you can find the admin password in SSM and use -W (uppercase) flag

time ldapsearch -w "$BIND_PASSWORD" -D cn=root,dc=moj,dc=com -LLL -H ldap:// -b ou=users,dc=moj,dc=com '+' '*' > /dev/null
or
time ldapsearch -D cn=root,dc=moj,dc=com -W -LLL -H ldap:// -b ou=users,dc=moj,dc=com '+' '*' > /dev/null
time ldapsearch -w "$BIND_PASSWORD" -D cn=root,dc=moj,dc=com -LLL -b ou=users,dc=moj,dc=com '(|(objectClass=NDRole)(objectClass=NDRoleAssociation))' '+' '*' > /dev/null

# dereferencing alias query
time ldapsearch -Y EXTERNAL -H ldapi://%2Fvar%2Flib%2Fopenldap%2Frun%2Fldapi -b 'cn=MarcusAspin,ou=Users,dc=moj,dc=com' -s one -a always '(|(objectClass=NDRole)(objectClass=NDRoleAssociation))'
time ldapsearch -Y EXTERNAL -H ldapi://%2Fvar%2Flib%2Fopenldap%2Frun%2Fldapi -b 'cn=MarcusAspin,ou=Users,dc=moj,dc=com' -s one -a never '(|(objectClass=NDRole)(objectClass=NDRoleAssociation))'
time ldapsearch -Y EXTERNAL -H ldapi://%2Fvar%2Flib%2Fopenldap%2Frun%2Fldapi -b 'cn=MarcusAspin,ou=Users,dc=moj,dc=com' -s one '(|(objectClass=NDRole)(objectClass=NDRoleAssociation))'
time ldapsearch -Y external -Q -H ldapi:// -b cn=marcusaspin,ou=users,dc=moj,dc=com objectclass=NDRoleAssociation > /dev/null
time ldapsearch -Y EXTERNAL -H ldapi:/// -b "cn=ndRoleCatalogue,ou=users,dc=moj,dc=com" "(&(objectclass=NDRole)(objectclass=*))"

# and some deref alias queries
time ldapsearch -H ldapi:// -Y EXTERNAL -Q -LLL -b "ou=Groups,dc=moj,dc=com" | grep -c ^dn:
time ldapsearch -H ldapi:// -Y EXTERNAL -Q -LLL -b "ou=Groups,dc=moj,dc=com" -a always | grep -c ^dn:
time ldapsearch -H ldapi:// -Y EXTERNAL -Q -LLL -b "ou=Groups,dc=moj,dc=com" -a never | grep -c ^dn:

#some user fetch queries to run
time ldapsearch -Y external -Q -H ldapi:// -LLL -b cn=juu31f,ou=users,dc=moj,dc=com -s one -a always '(|(objectClass=NDRole)(objectClass=NDRoleAssociation))' UIBusinessInteractionCollection Level1 Level2 Level3
time ldapsearch -Y external -Q -H ldapi:// -LLL -b cn=juu31f,ou=users,dc=moj,dc=com -s base -a always '(objectclass=*)' userHomeArea userSector mail telephoneNumber
time ldapsearch -Y external -Q -H ldapi:// -LLL -b cn=UserPreferences,cn=juu31f,ou=users,dc=moj,dc=com -s base -a always '(objectclass=*)'
```

> **Important:** Cache warming is a required part of the LDAP restart procedure. Do not consider the restart is complete until the cache-warming process has successfully completed

--- 

## 7. Verify LDAP is Operational

After cache warming has completed, verify that the LDAP service is operating normally

Confirm that:

- The ECS service has **1 desired task**
- The LDAP task is **running**
- The task is healhty
- Cache warming completed successfully
- There are no unexpected errors or task restarts

